{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_169","type":"command_execution","command":"\"D:\\\\software\\\\PowerShell\\\\pwsh-7.6.6\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$a=\"D:'\"\\\\tmp\\\\rsi-tf0604-run5\\\\trials\\\\tf-0285-l03-baseline-3\\\\agent\\\"; Get-Content \\\"\"'$a'\"\\\\.gitattributes\\\" -Raw\"","aggregated_output":"# VerseShell process-lifecycle patch is content-addressed by the committed\n# manifest (provenance.build_input.diff_sha256 / compliance checksum) and\n# verified by tests/unit/uas-05-verseshell-process-lifecycle.test.ts and\n# tests/unit/verseshell-manifest.test.ts. It must be checked out byte-identical\n# to the blob on every platform; core.autocrlf=true would otherwise smudge it\n# to CRLF on fresh worktrees and break the recorded SHA-256.\nresources/verseshell/patches/uas-05-process-lifecycle.patch -text\n\n# RC-00 acceptance reconstructs VerseShell in a detached worktree on Windows where\n# core.autocrlf=true would smudge these ordered patch files from LF to CRLF,\n# breaking the byte-size / SHA-256 check in scripts/verseshell-bundle.mjs\n# (root cause of the provision-verseshell-resources gate fail recorded in\n# artifacts/unblock-pack/tf0020-h01-nogo.md). Pin all ordered patches to LF bytes\n# on every checkout.\nresources/verseshell/patches/*.patch -text\n\n# RC-01 acceptance uses this generated inventory as a candidate-bound input.\n# Keep the JSON byte-stable across Windows and POSIX checkouts so rerunning its\n# deterministic generator cannot create an EOL-only worktree mutation.\nartifacts/runtime-authority-convergence/rc-01/baseline.json -text\n\n# TF-0009 closure verifies exact report and manifest bytes on every platform.\nartifacts/first-product-preview/TF-0009/** -text\n# Task Forest repair files and evidence are hashed in the closeout manifest.\nartifacts/task-forest-landing-20260930/** -text\n.codex-tools/task-forest/** -text\n\n# Static-integrity generated artifacts are byte-compared by the runtime check\n# guards (npm shrinkwrap guard, tool display, host env policy). core.autocrlf\n# would smudge them to CRLF in fresh detached acceptance worktrees and make the\n# byte comparison fail, so pin them to the committed LF bytes like the other\n# content-addressed generated files above.\nopenclaw_runtime/npm-shrinkwrap.json -text\nopenclaw_runtime/extensions/*/npm-shrinkwrap.json -text\nopenclaw_runtime/apps/shared/OpenClawKit/Sources/OpenClawKit/Resources/tool-display.json -text\nopenclaw_runtime/apps/macos/Sources/OpenClaw/HostEnvSecurityPolicy.generated.swift -text\n\n# Preserve the complete VerseConf delivery bytes used by its SHA-256 manifest.\nopenclaw_runtime/extensions/verseconf-artifacts/vendor/verseconf/** -text\n\n# These historical acceptance blobs are hash-locked CRLF. Preserve their bytes;\n# keep the normal whitespace checks while recognizing the CRLF line endings.\nartifacts/runtime-test-integrity/report.json -text whitespace=blank-at-eol,blank-at-eof,space-before-tab,cr-at-eol\nartifacts/runtime-test-integrity/credential-scan.json -text whitespace=blank-at-eol,blank-at-eof,space-before-tab,cr-at-eol\nartifacts/runtime-test-integrity/SHA256SUMS -text whitespace=blank-at-eol,blank-at-eof,space-before-tab,cr-at-eol\n\n# Current desktop acceptance evidence is byte-addressed on every checkout.\nartifacts/desktop-acceptance-followups/* -text\nartifacts/frozen-windows-acceptance-20261007/* -text\nartifacts/windows-delivery-blocker-fixes/* -text\nartifacts/windows-alpha-closeout-20261008/* -text\n# Historical curated inputs retain their original bytes; they are not new verdicts.\nartifacts/uas-06-single-local-exec-canary/live-observations.json -text whitespace=blank-at-eol,blank-at-eof,space-before-tab,cr-at-eol\nartifacts/agent-engineering-acceptance/runtime-authority-convergence-final/human-verdict.yaml -text whitespace=blank-at-eol,blank-at-eof,space-before-tab,cr-at-eol\n\nartifacts/stepfun-basic-live-evidence-20261008/* -text\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
